      "title": "Student Life",
      "value": "<p>The college's 100-acre flagship campus in Barrie is just an hour north of Toronto. Georgian College has an inclusive and diverse outlook. From arrival, students are supported so they can settle into college life. The establishment offers individualised orientation and mentoring services so international students can feel at home.&nbsp;</p><p>Moreover, across the six campus locations in the Georgian Bay area, students will experience a fun community lifestyle. Social, academic, cultural, and sports clubs are available at various campuses too. Also, students can take part in regular on-campus events and socials, run by the Georgian College Students' Association (GCSA).</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>At Georgian College of Applied Arts and Technology, students have several on-campus and off-campus housing options. First, students can select the on-campus accommodation option. However, these are only available for those located at the Barrie, Orillia and Owen Sound campuses. Alternatively, the college can support students with finding a landlord or host family to stay with off-campus. Georgina staff also have resources and tips available to help you safely find somewhere to stay off campus.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Library",
      "value": "<p>Across its six campuses, Georgian has a range of modern leisure and academic facilities. First, students can access IT services and libraries at five campuses. Among the library resources are subject-specific books, online databases, ebooks and academic support. The college also has modern classrooms and teaching facilities and some practical learning areas.</p>",
